WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.594 --> 00:00:04.487
Show comparables.

00:00:05.192 --> 00:00:07.841
If you’re trying to raise money off an idea

00:00:08.277 --> 00:00:09.403
that other people have done before

00:00:09.622 --> 00:00:11.036
or you’re trying to buy into a current system

00:00:11.263 --> 00:00:14.252
show comparables so it makes the decisions

00:00:14.421 --> 00:00:16.224
easier for an investor to say yes.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.576
One of the hardest things for the investors

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:19.581
to say yes to

00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:22.731
is risk, right.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:24.861
If you are the first person to try to do something

00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:26.617
there’s a lot of risk attached to it

00:00:26.876 --> 00:00:28.733
and so there might be a lot of opportunity

00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:30.024
but then there’s a lot of risk.

00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:32.123
And so it’s hard for them to say yes.

00:00:32.895 --> 00:00:33.752
But if you can show them

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:34.769
that this has been done before

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:36.384
and the kind of numbers that it generates

00:00:36.646 --> 00:00:38.468
then it’s easier for them to say yes

00:00:38.709 --> 00:00:40.167
because they have a clear understanding

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:40.842
of the opportunity

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.085
and they know what risk level is.

00:00:43.664 --> 00:00:45.652
So reduce the risk by showing comparables.

00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:47.340
I got a great question from one of my

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:47.943
YouTube viewers

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:48.592
(love you guys!)

00:00:49.175 --> 00:00:50.239
JawwCracker

00:00:50.331 --> 00:00:52.332
and JawwCracker is trying to raise money.

00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:54.515
He wants to start a kiosk in a mall around

00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:56.611
the Tommie Copper product.

00:00:57.276 --> 00:00:59.065
I’ve never hear of Tommie Copper but that’s cool.

00:01:00.242 --> 00:01:01.067
So to get this thing going

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.119
you want to raise this money

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.292
you want to create this business plan

00:01:05.396 --> 00:01:06.753
show me some comparables.

00:01:07.194 --> 00:01:09.823
Show me who else has done a Tommie Copper kiosk

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:11.552
how much money they’re making

00:01:11.856 --> 00:01:13.584
how much their cost are

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:16.812
and how their location is relevant to mine.

00:01:17.472 --> 00:01:18.894
That’s what investors are going to look at.

00:01:19.168 --> 00:01:21.980
It’s going to be a pretty simple calculation.

00:01:22.547 --> 00:01:23.611
Okay, that other kiosk;

00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:24.719
how much is it making

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:26.771
how much are they spending

00:01:27.595 --> 00:01:29.086
and how does the mall that they’re in

00:01:29.086 --> 00:01:30.342
compare to the mall that you want to go to?

00:01:30.955 --> 00:01:31.892
If those numbers work out

00:01:32.419 --> 00:01:33.376
it’s easy to say yes.

00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:34.582
If they don’t work out

00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:36.624
then it’s going to be a lot harder

00:01:36.624 --> 00:01:37.267
to raise the money.

00:01:37.486 --> 00:01:38.350
This might even be something

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.214
that the banks would look at

00:01:39.614 --> 00:01:40.479
depending on how

00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:42.592
your relationship is with your bank manager.

00:01:43.724 --> 00:01:44.882
If I was financing this

00:01:46.622 --> 00:01:48.796
it depends on the investor you’re going after.

00:01:49.036 --> 00:01:51.264
This is not a venture capital type of investment.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:54.410
This is more an angel investor

00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:56.952
but not even a strategic angel investor.

00:01:57.552 --> 00:01:59.242
It’s just somebody to give you money.

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.312
And this could be in the form of a loan.

00:02:01.876 --> 00:02:03.572
If you want something to be in like

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.022
the 10-15% interest rate.

00:02:06.303 --> 00:02:07.384
They give you the money

00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:09.210
and you create your location

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:09.744
and go from there.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.291
If you can get a strategic angel investor to come in

00:02:13.652 --> 00:02:14.805
and put some experience

00:02:15.456 --> 00:02:17.140
to help you grow this thing to multiple locations

00:02:17.313 --> 00:02:18.312
that’s a bonus.

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:22.268
But I think you’re looking at just a guy with money.

00:02:22.558 --> 00:02:23.660
You’re looking at, like a dentist

00:02:23.886 --> 00:02:24.922
a doctor, a lawyer

00:02:25.192 --> 00:02:26.755
who wants a hands-off investment

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:29.916
where they can get a premium return on a loan

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:30.648
that they’re giving you.

00:02:30.648 --> 00:02:31.821
It’s probably your best bet.

00:02:31.821 --> 00:02:33.011
And for them to say yes

00:02:33.588 --> 00:02:35.194
show them comparables of people

00:02:35.194 --> 00:02:36.691
who’ve done it before.

00:02:36.691 --> 00:02:37.638
Believe.

